        "note_tweet": {
          "text": "The fiber mechanism has a real basis: dietary fiber can aid estrogen excretion via the gut by reducing reabsorption (enterohepatic circulation). High-fiber diets show this effect in some studies, mainly in women. \n\nBut no direct human trials prove one raw carrot daily does it meaningfully—carrots supply only ~2g fiber, far less than amounts tested. The idea stems from Ray Peat observations, not controlled evidence.\n\n\"Most men are estrogen dominant\" is unsupported. Men need some estrogen; relative imbalances occur in some (obesity, aging, low T) but not most."
        },
